---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import InnerOverlays from '../components/InnerOverlays.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const updated = '17 November 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site does and does not collect: no cookies, no analytics, no tracking. A plain account of the few requests your browser makes."
>
  <main id="main" class="page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">home</a> / <span aria-current="page">privacy</span>
      </nav>
      <header class="page-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
        <h1>What this site knows about you</h1>
        <p>
          Very little, and none of it on purpose. This page says exactly what happens when you open it — written
          plainly, because a privacy notice nobody can read protects nobody.
        </p>
        <p class="stamp">Updated {updated}</p>
      </header>

      <article class="case">
        <section class="v-sec">
          <h2 class="v-h">
            <span>The short version</span>
            <small>01</small>
          </h2>
          <ul class="feat grid2">
            <li>No cookies are set by this site.</li>
            <li>No analytics, no tracking pixels, no advertising, no session recording.</li>
            <li>No account to create, and nothing you type is stored on a server.</li>
            <li>Nothing is shared with or sold to anybody.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="v-sec">
          <h2 class="v-h">
            <span>What your browser stores</span>
            <small>02</small>
          </h2>
          <p>
            Nothing. The site has one appearance — black and gold, taken from my logo — so there is no setting to
            remember. An earlier version of this site saved a light-or-dark choice in your browser under the name{' '}
            <code>theme</code>; that is no longer used, and the site now deletes it the first time you visit.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="v-sec">
          <h2 class="v-h">
            <span>Requests your browser makes</span>
            <small>03</small>
          </h2>
          <p>
            The pages are static files, but three requests go to other companies. They will see your IP address, as any
            web request does.
          </p>
          <dl class="v-meta wide">
            <div>
              <dt>The host</dt>
              <dd>
                The pages, images and PDFs are served by this site's hosting provider, which keeps short-lived server
                logs of requests (IP address, page, time) for security and troubleshooting. I do not read them for
                analytics.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Google Fonts</dt>
              <dd>
                The three typefaces are loaded from <code>fonts.googleapis.com</code> and
                <code>fonts.gstatic.com</code>, so Google receives the request for the font files. If you would rather
                that did not happen, a font blocker or a strict privacy extension will stop it and the site still works.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>GitHub</dt>
              <dd>
                The home page shows my live repository count and languages, which it reads from GitHub's public API when
                you reach that section, so GitHub sees that request. With JavaScript off, the panel simply says it could
                not load.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <section class="v-sec">
          <h2 class="v-h">
            <span>The forms</span>
            <small>04</small>
          </h2>
          <p>
            The message form and the booking form do not send anything anywhere by themselves. They check what you have
            typed in your browser, then open your own e-mail app or WhatsApp with the message already written, and you
            decide whether to send it. Until you press send in that app, nothing has left your device.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you do send it, I receive it the ordinary way — as an e-mail at {site.email} or a WhatsApp message on
            {site.phone} — and I keep it only as long as I need it to reply and to keep a record of the work.
          </p>
          <p class="art-note">
            This will change later: the message form is being given a proper send button that posts to a small function
            on this site's own domain, with a spam check. When that happens, this page will be updated to say exactly
            what the function stores and for how long.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="v-sec">
          <h2 class="v-h">
            <span>Links away from here</span>
            <small>05</small>
          </h2>
          <p>
            Project demos, GitHub, LinkedIn, X and WhatsApp are other people's services with their own privacy policies.
            Opening them is a normal visit to those sites, and what they collect is up to them.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="v-sec">
          <h2 class="v-h">
            <span>Children, and your rights</span>
            <small>06</small>
          </h2>
          <p>
            This site is not aimed at children and collects nothing from anyone. Since there is no database and no
            account, there is nothing of yours to download, correct or delete. If you have written to me and want our
            correspondence deleted, ask and I will delete it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="v-sec">
          <h2 class="v-h">
            <span>Who to ask</span>
            <small>07</small>
          </h2>
          <p>
            This site belongs to Akanji Oluwaseun Gabriel (asgatcreation), {site.location}. Questions about this page,
            or anything on the site:
          </p>
          <div class="v-ctas">
            <a class="btn gold" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>
              Email me
            </a>
            <a class="btn" href={`https://wa.me/${site.whatsapp}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              WhatsApp ↗
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="art-note">
            The site's code is public, so you do not have to take my word for any of this — you can read it.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <InnerOverlays slot="overlays" />
  <script src="../scripts/site.js"></script>
</Base>
